**When to read this file:** When you add or gate code that touches files, network, OS, hardware, UI, or security — and always when you edit `std/src/ooda/` (see `BOOTSTRAP.oot` tier *Security, sandboxing, capability gating* + `DESIGN.oot` §3).

*Update this list when a token is added or fractured. Keep count note in sync with DESIGN. Prefer granular tokens in new APIs; do not claim op-level granular enforce until CAP-G* lands.*
